kaleidoscope_fishing.journal.tide_help_high=High tide comes around dawn and around dusk, a little later each day. Big sea fish (tuna, skipjack, grouper, hairtail, anglerfish) bite more.
kaleidoscope_fishing.journal.tide_help_low=At low tide, crabs and oysters bite more, and twice as much wet sand bubbles on the beach. Dig a bubbling spot with a shovel.
kaleidoscope_fishing.journal.tide_help_moon=On a full-moon night, Moon Jellyfish rise in the sea and Glow Crabs come up the beach.
kaleidoscope_fishing.journal.end_hint=In the End, any water holds fish. With an Ender Fishing Rod you can also cast off an island's edge into the void.
